{
  "note": "Fish-folk: a person's frame with a fish's head on it, which is the only way this reads at the distance the camera watches from. The silhouette does the work — a crest down the skull, a snout instead of a face and a fin on each forearm — and the colours are the ones a fish is, not the ones a man is.",
  "parts": [
    { "note": "The skull, longer than a man's, with the snout carried forward.", "box": [0.4, 0.28, 0.26], "at": [0.04, 1.28, 0], "color": "#ffffff", "tint": 0, "anim": "head", "pivot": [0, 1.12, 0] },
